<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry III, Landgrave of Hesse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1440–<a href="/years/1483">1483</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Henry the Rich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry III (1440–1483), called the Rich, was Landgrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hesse">Upper Hesse</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marburg">Marburg</a> after the division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> in 1458. Through his marriage to Anna of Katzenelnbogen he inherited the wealthy County of Katzenelnbogen in 1479, with its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> tolls and the area around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>. His lands were reunited with Lower Hesse in 1500 under his nephew William II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-iii-landgrave-of-hesse.jpg" alt="Henry III, Landgrave of Hesse" width="160" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrichiiilandgrafhessen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
